{{!-- A compact archive row: the text block against a small fixed thumbnail on the right.

	{{> "archive/row"}}                                    the tag archive's
	{{> "archive/row" tagEyebrow=true titleClass="text-[25px] leading-[1.2]" padding="py-[30px]"}}
	                                                       the author archive's

	tagEyebrow   lead with the post's primary tag in the accent, and sign off with the date
	titleClass   headline size — 26px on the tag archive, 25px on the author archive
	padding      row padding — 32px on the tag archive, 30px on the author archive

Shared by the tag archive and the author archive, which is how the design draws them: one row,
differing only in which of the two meta facts leads and which signs off. On a tag archive every
row already carries the tag, so the date leads and the writer signs; on an author archive every
row is by the same writer, so the tag leads and the date signs. The same trade the reference
build makes in src/components/PostListRow.astro.

Called from inside {{#foreach posts}}, so the post is the context and a partial's hash arguments
are merged into it — `tagEyebrow` is a plain read, no `../`.

The whole row is ONE link, unlike the Feed's wide row, because the design draws it that way: no
second link to the same place means nothing to hide from assistive technology, and the image
takes an empty alt because the headline inside the same link already names the destination.

A post with no feature image drops the second column rather than leaving a 132px gutter beside
it. Both class lists are written out in full — a class assembled at render time is one Tailwind's
scanner never compiles. --}}
<article class="{{post_class}} border-border border-b">
	<a
		href="{{url}}"
		class="text-text no-underline {{#if feature_image}}max-stack:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)] max-stack:gap-4 grid grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_132px] items-start gap-8{{else}}block{{/if}} {{#if padding}}{{padding}}{{else}}py-8{{/if}}">
		<div>
			<div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
				{{#if tagEyebrow}}
					{{#primary_tag}}
						<span class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-accent uppercase">{{name}}</span>
					{{/primary_tag}}
				{{else}}
					<span class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-muted uppercase">{{date format="DD MMM YYYY"}}</span>
				{{/if}}

				{{> "tier-chip"}}
			</div>

			<h2
				class="font-display tracking-heading mt-2.5 font-medium {{#if titleClass}}{{titleClass}}{{else}}text-[26px] leading-[1.2]{{/if}}">{{title}}</h2>

			{{#if excerpt}}
				<p class="text-small text-muted mt-2.5 max-w-[64ch] leading-[1.6] text-pretty">{{excerpt}}</p>
			{{/if}}

			<p class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-muted mt-3 uppercase">
				{{#if tagEyebrow}}
					{{~date format="DD MMM YYYY"~}}
				{{else}}
					{{~> "byline"~}}
				{{/if}}
				<span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
				{{~reading_time seconds=(t "< 1 min read") minute=(t "1 min read") minutes=(t "% min read")~}}
			</p>
		</div>

		{{#if feature_image}}
			<img
				src="{{img_url feature_image size="s"}}"
				{{#if feature_image_alt}}alt="{{feature_image_alt}}"{{else}}alt=""{{/if}}
				width="132"
				height="99"
				loading="lazy"
				decoding="async"
				class="border-border block h-[99px] w-[132px] rounded-sm border object-cover">
		{{/if}}
	</a>
</article>
